# Platform shell navigation

Cross-origin navigation between **WebOnOne (core shell)** and **peer microservice FEs** (Identity profile, Email, Data) uses **two channels**. Pick the channel by who owns the chrome.

## Embed channel (WebOnOne — iframe in `#main-content`)

When **WebOnOne** owns the shell (sidebar + header), load peer pages **in-place** via iframe — no full-page redirect.

```text
WebOnOne AppLayout (sidebar + header stay mounted; embedMain on AppShell)
  → navigate(sentinel path: /email/*, /data/*, /profile)
  → PlatformPeerFrame → PlatformServiceFrame
  → POST /auth/code with redirectUri = {peerOrigin}{path} only (no embed query)
  → iframe src = peer path + ?embed=platform&parentOrigin&core_nav&theme&code

Peer AppLayout (embed=platform + validated parentOrigin, or iframe + session)
  → ensurePlatformEmbedCanvas() in main.tsx (full-height #root before paint)
  → PlatformEmbedLayout (chromeless Outlet — no AppShell)
  → usePlatformSessionBootstrap (code exchange) + usePlatformEmbedListener (JWT sync)
  → FeaturePage + ListPageBody flex fill; pagination mt-auto at bottom
```

| WebOnOne uses embed (local `navigate`) | Use redirect (auth-code `window.location.assign`) |
|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Left-nav Email/Data sentinels | Satellite standalone bookmark / direct URL |
| Header **Profile** (`/profile` sentinel) | Satellite-to-satellite hops (Data ↔ Email, satellite → Profile) |
| Any new core-shell peer sentinel | Login / OAuth callback flows |

**Package:** `@webonone/platform-embed` — `ensurePlatformEmbedCanvas`, `buildPlatformEmbedUrl`, `PlatformServiceFrame`, `PlatformEmbedShell`, `usePlatformEmbedListener`, `resolvePlatformEmbedParentOrigin`.

**Consumer (WebOnOne):** `features/shell/pages/PlatformPeerFrame.tsx`; routes `email/*`, `data/*`, `profile/*` in `app/router.tsx`. Nav sentinels + header profile use `onNavItemNavigate` / `navigate` only — **no** `onClick` redirect on core shell.

**Peers (Identity, Email, Data):** early `embed=platform` branch in `app/AppLayout.tsx` → `features/auth/components/PlatformEmbedLayout.tsx`. `hasAnyPlatformHandoff` allows embed (`code` + `embed=platform`) or redirect (`code` + `return_url`).

**Layout / height (embed):** `ensurePlatformEmbedCanvas()` full-height `#root`. **`PlatformEmbedShell` `<main>`** scrolls (`overflow-y-auto scrollbar-themed`). Page chain uses **`min-h-full`** so short content fills the iframe and **`Pagination` `mt-auto`** stays at the bottom; tall content grows the page and scrolls on `<main>`.

### Embed page content (required — all peer FEs)

Every route inside `PlatformEmbedLayout` **must** use **`FeaturePage`** (`shellPagePadding`).

| Concern | Rule |
|---------|------|
| **Fill height** | `platform-embed-outlet` → `FeaturePage` → `.feature-page-body` → `ListPageBody` — **`min-h-full` / `flex-1`** chain (embed CSS in `globals.css`) |
| **Pagination bottom** | `ListPageBody` + list in `flex-1` + `Pagination className="mt-auto"` — same markup as standalone |
| **Scroll** | **Only** on `.platform-embed-shell-main` when content exceeds iframe — **never** `overflow-auto` on list wrappers |

```tsx
<FeaturePage title="Tags" …>
  <ListPageBody>
    <div className="flex-1"><ItemList … /></div>
    <Pagination className="mt-auto" … />
  </ListPageBody>
</FeaturePage>
```

**Forbidden in embed peers:** `overflow-auto` on list/table sub-regions; outlet/page roots without `min-h-full` flex chain; bare `<div>` instead of `FeaturePage`.

**CSP:** peer `vite.config.ts` `frame-ancestors` includes `VITE_WEBONONE_ORIGIN`. Identity/Email/Data: `VITE_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS` for `parentOrigin` validation.

**Auth-code `redirectUri`:** `{peerOrigin}{path}` only — embed query params are **not** part of `redirectUri`.

## Redirect channel (satellite full-page handoff)

When a **satellite** opens another service (or user bookmarks a peer URL), use auth-code redirect:

```text
Consumer AppLayout
  → useServiceRedirect().redirect(get<Peer>RedirectOptions(...))
  → Identity POST /auth/code (Bearer JWT)
  → window.location.assign(peerUrl?code&return_url&core_nav)

Destination AppLayout
  → PageShell + <Outlet /> while !authenticated (platform handoff)
  → AppShell + core nav when authenticated && return_url

Destination home PAGE (not AppLayout, not /callback)
  → read ?code (skip if hasPlatformEmbedHandoff — embed uses usePlatformSessionBootstrap in PlatformEmbedLayout)
  → bootstrap session → dispatch login → strip code from URL
  → unified AppLayout overlay for loading — [loading-empty-states.mdc](loading-empty-states.mdc)
```

## Three layers — same structure every time

| Layer | Responsibility | Profile | Email | Data |
|-------|----------------|---------|-------|------|
| **1. WebOnOne outbound (embed)** | Local navigate to sentinel | `AppLayout` `handleProfileClick` → `navigate('/profile')` | sentinels via `onNavItemNavigate` | sentinels via `onNavItemNavigate` |
| **1b. Satellite outbound (redirect)** | Auth-code full page | `redirectToIdentityProfile.ts` | `redirectToEmail.ts` | `redirectToData.ts` |
| **2. Peer layout** | Embed branch + shell split | `identity/.../app/AppLayout.tsx` | `email/.../app/AppLayout.tsx` | `data/.../app/AppLayout.tsx` |
| **3. Peer page** | Redirect bootstrap only (not embed) | `ProfilePage.tsx` | `DashboardPage.tsx` | list pages |

Supporting utils (same roles — mirror naming):

| Role | Profile (reference) | Email (mirror) | New satellite |
|------|---------------------|----------------|---------------|
| Exchange code for JWT | `bootstrapProfileSession.ts` | `bootstrapPlatformSession.ts` | `bootstrap<Name>Session.ts` on home feature |
| Parse / strip `return_url` | `profileReturn.ts` | `platformReturn.ts` | `<name>Return.ts` or shared pattern |
| Home `redirectUri` getter | `profileConfig.ts` → `getIdentityProfileRedirectUri()` | `bootstrapPlatformSession.ts` → `getEmailHomeRedirectUri()` | `get<Name>HomeRedirectUri()` |
| Core nav in platform mode | `shell/config/navItems.ts` `buildCoreNavFromQuery` | `shell/config/coreNavItems.ts` + `buildAppNav.ts` | `buildCoreNav*` in `AppLayout` |
| Outbound profile | — (is profile host) | `redirectToIdentityProfile.ts` | `redirectToIdentityProfile.ts` |
| Consumer peer config | `identityConfig.ts` | `emailConfig.ts` | `<peer>Config.ts` |

## Consumer `AppLayout` (WebOnOne core shell)

**Embed peers (Email, Data, Profile from WebOnOne):**

1. Sentinel routes in `app/router.tsx` → `PlatformPeerFrame` (`peer`: `email` | `data` | `identity`).
2. `isPlatformPeerEmbedPath` → `AppShell` `embedMain={true}` (iframe fills `#main-content`, parent scrolls).
3. `createNavItemNavigate` for sidebar; `handleProfileClick` → `navigate('/profile')` — **no** `useServiceRedirect` on core shell.
4. Sentinels in `@webonone/platform-nav`: `EMAIL_NAV_SENTINELS`, `DATA_NAV_SENTINELS`, `PROFILE_NAV_SENTINEL` (`/profile`).

**Reference:** `webonone-v2/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `features/shell/pages/PlatformPeerFrame.tsx`.

## Consumer `AppLayout` (satellite → peer redirect)

**Required for satellite-to-satellite hops:**

1. `useServiceRedirect()` hook.
2. `get<Peer>RedirectOptions({ accessToken, returnUrl, navVariant, extraSearchParams? })` with `authCodeEndpoint`, peer home `targetUrl`, `returnUrl`, `core_nav`, theme params.
3. Handler calls `redirect(options)` — nav `onClick` on peer items.
4. Profile from satellite: `redirectToIdentityProfile` (full page — not embed).

**Reference:** `email/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx` `handleProfileClick`; `data/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx` `handleProfileClick`.

## Destination `AppLayout` (peer FE — Identity, Email, Data)

**Embed branch (first):** `resolvePlatformEmbedParentOrigin` → `PlatformEmbedLayout` + `PLATFORM_EMBED_APP_HOST_CLASS`. `ensurePlatformEmbedCanvas()` in `main.tsx`.

**Redirect / standalone branch:**

1. Parse `return_url` from query (allowlisted).
2. Core nav when `return_url` present.
3. `AppShell` when platform context + authenticated (or handoff); else `PageShell`.
4. Satellite platform shell: `onProfileClick` → `redirectToIdentityProfile` (full page).

**Do not** bootstrap JWT in non-embed `AppLayout` shell branch. Embed bootstrap lives in `PlatformEmbedLayout` → `usePlatformSessionBootstrap`.

## Logout (satellite FE in platform shell)

When the user signs out from a satellite opened with `return_url` (core shell mode), send them to the **parent core `/login`**, not the satellite's local login page.

**Required in every satellite `AppLayout` `handleLogout`:**

1. Resolve effective `return_url` from query **or** persisted platform context (Email: `platform.returnUrl`).
2. Clear satellite auth storage synchronously (`clearEmailAuthStorage`, `persistAuthSession(null)`, etc.).
3. `performPlatformLogout(returnUrl)` from `@webonone/platform-nav` — uses `window.location.replace` to core `{origin}/login`.
4. **Do not** `dispatch(logout())` before redirect — that re-renders the satellite `/login` route and flashes the wrong page.
5. No `return_url` → `performPlatformLogout` falls back to local `'/login'` (standalone mode).

**Reference:** `email/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`, `identity/frontend/src/app/AppLayout.tsx`.

## Destination home page (redirect handoff only)

When `hasPlatformEmbedHandoff` — **skip** page-level code bootstrap (handled in `PlatformEmbedLayout`).

**Redirect handoff — match `ProfilePage.tsx` pattern:**

1. `const code = searchParams.get('code')`; skip when `hasPlatformEmbedHandoff(searchParams)`.
2. Single bootstrap `useEffect` when `code` + `return_url` handoff.
3. `usePlatformLoading` for overlay — no inline `LoadingState` copy in page content.
4. `if (!accessToken && !code) return <Navigate to="/login" />`

## Satellite peer nav (cross-satellite core menu)

When a satellite renders core nav, **peer service links** must not resolve to `{coreOrigin}/email/...` or `{coreOrigin}/data/...`.

**Required on each satellite:**

1. **Peer origin env** — one `VITE_<PEER>_ORIGIN` per connected satellite (Data: `VITE_EMAIL_ORIGIN`; Email: `VITE_DATA_ORIGIN`).
2. **`resolvePlatformNavUrls`** — pass own origin for self in the peer map (`{ email: emailOrigin }` or `{ data: dataOrigin }`).
3. **Rewrite own links** — `rewriteEmailOriginLinks` / `rewriteDataOriginLinks` so local routes use relative paths.
4. **Outbound peer clicks** — `withEmailNavActions` / `withDataNavActions` on core nav + `handleEmailNavClick` / `handleDataNavClick` calling `getEmailRedirectOptions` / `getDataRedirectOptions` with nav sentinel (auth-code redirect — same as WebOnOne consumer).

| Satellite | Peer config | Redirect | Nav wiring |
|-----------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Data | `features/email/utils/emailConfig.ts` | `redirectToEmail.ts` | `shell/utils/externalNavActions.ts`, `AppLayout` `handleEmailNavClick` |
| Email | `features/data/utils/dataConfig.ts` | `redirectToData.ts` | `shell/utils/externalNavActions.ts`, `AppLayout` `handleDataNavClick` |

**Forbidden:** core-origin hrefs for authenticated peer navigation from a satellite; `navigate()` to peer paths on the wrong origin.

## `PrivateRoute`

Allow route when `accessToken` **or** `hasAnyPlatformHandoff(searchParams)` — platform redirect (`code` + validated `return_url`) **or** iframe embed (`code` + `embed=platform` + validated `parentOrigin`), no `state`. Never flash `/login` during handoff.

## Routes

| Route | Use |
|-------|-----|
| Peer **home** (`/profile`, `/`, …) | Platform inbound handoff + page bootstrap |
| `/callback` | **Standalone OAuth only** (`code` + `state`) — never platform handoff |
| `/go/*`, `*RedirectPage` | **Forbidden** on consumer |

## `targetUrl` / `redirectUri` pairs (must match exchange)

| Peer | `targetUrl` / `redirectUri` |
|------|----------------------------|
| Identity profile | `{identityOrigin}/profile` |
| Email home | `{emailOrigin}/` |
| New satellite | `{serviceOrigin}/<home-path>` |

Identity `ALLOWED_REDIRECT_URIS` must include each home URI.

## Scaffolding checklist (new satellite with platform shell)

Copy Profile roles row-by-row from tables above:

- [ ] `features/<peer>/utils/redirectTo<Peer>.ts` on **each consumer** FE
- [ ] Consumer `AppLayout`: `handle<Peer>Click` + `redirect()` (nav `onClick` or header)
- [ ] `features/<home>/utils/bootstrap<Name>Session.ts`
- [ ] `features/<home>/utils/<name>Return.ts` (`parseReturnUrl`, `stripAuthCodeFromSearch` wrapper)
- [ ] `<Home>Page.tsx` with Profile-shaped bootstrap `useEffect`
- [ ] `app/AppLayout.tsx` with Profile-shaped shell split
- [ ] `PrivateRoute` + `hasPlatformHandoff`
- [ ] `redirectToIdentityProfile.ts` on satellite for profile header
- [ ] `packages/platform-nav/src/coreNav.ts` leaf + `externalService` if core menu item
- [ ] Consumer `features/<peer>/utils/<peer>Config.ts` — origin only; derive home/callback in code
- [ ] Satellite `VITE_<PEER>_ORIGIN` + outbound peer redirect when core nav includes other satellites
- [ ] `PlatformLoadingProvider` + unified overlay in `AppLayout` — [loading-empty-states.mdc](loading-empty-states.mdc)
- [ ] Embed channel: `PlatformEmbedLayout`, `ensurePlatformEmbedCanvas` in `main.tsx`, `VITE_WEBONONE_ORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors`, `@webonone/platform-embed` on consumer + peer
- [ ] WebOnOne: sentinel route + `PlatformPeerFrame` peer id; `PROFILE_NAV_SENTINEL` in `platform-nav` if profile host

## Forbidden

- `/go/*` routes or `*RedirectPage` components on consumer ("Opening …" spinners)
- Platform handoff to `/callback` or `AuthLayout`
- JWT bootstrap in `AppLayout` instead of home page
- Raw `VITE_*_ORIGIN` hrefs for authenticated peers
- `PrivateRoute` → `/login` during valid `code` + `return_url` handoff
- Different flow for Email vs Profile vs the next service — **one pattern only**
- Inline session/page `"Loading…"` text or per-route overlay spinners — use unified overlay instead

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root
npm run type-check -w identity-root
npm run type-check -w email-root
```

Manual: WebOnOne → Profile, Email, Data — shell persists, iframe loads peer, pagination at bottom on list pages. Satellite → Profile still full-page redirect.
